t a glance</b></h2>\n  <p class=\"pir-lede\">Sea bass at the Rungis wholesale market closes week 39 at €8.77/kg, virtually unchanged on the week; on the month it is up 5.5%. Against the same period of 2025 the price is 6.4% higher. For late September it is the highest level of the last five years. Over the last twelve months Italy imported 28,199 tonnes, 54% of it from Greece.</p>\n  <table class=\"pir-tabella\">\n    <caption>Last twelve weeks. FranceAgriMer, RNM Rungis.</caption>\n    <thead><tr><th>Week</th><th>€/kg</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody><tr><td>2026-W28</td><td>7.31</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W29</td><td>7.41</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W30</td><td>7.55</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W31</td><td>7.57</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W32</td><td>7.91</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W33</td><td>8.06</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W34</td><td>8.13</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W35</td><td>8.31</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W36</td><td>8.52</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W37</td><td>8.77</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W38</td><td>8.79</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W39</td><td>8.77</td></tr></tbody>\n  </table>\n  <dl class=\"pir-domande\"><dt>Why a French price?</dt><dd>There is no public weekly survey of sea bass prices in Italy. Rungis is the European wholesale market with the most continuous and documented survey.</dd></dl>\n</section>"}